     "text": "```python\ndef compute_mean_online(data_stream):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the mean of a data stream using an online algorithm.\n    \n    This function processes a sequence of numbers in a streaming fashion, maintaining\n    a running total and count to compute the mean incrementally. This approach is\n    efficient for large datasets as it does not require storing the entire dataset\n    in memory.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    data_stream (iterable): An iterable of numerical values representing the data stream.\n    \n    Returns:\n    float: The mean of the data stream.\n    \n    Raises:\n    ValueError: If the data stream is empty or contains non-numeric values.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = 0.0\n    count = 0\n    \n    for value in data_stream:\n        if not isinstance(value, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"All elements in the data stream must be numeric.\")\n        total += value\n        count += 1\n    \n    if count == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"The data stream cannot be empty.\")\n    \n    return total / count\n```",
