     "text": "```python\ndef compute_mean_online(stream):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the mean of a stream of numbers using an online algorithm.\n    \n    This function processes a sequence of numbers incrementally, maintaining a running\n    total and count of elements seen so far. The mean is calculated as the total\n    divided by the count at each step.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    stream (iterable): An iterable of numerical values (int or float).\n    \n    Returns:\n    float: The current mean of the processed elements.\n    \n    Note:\n    - This function is designed to handle large datasets efficiently by processing\n      data in a single pass without requiring storage of the entire dataset.\n    - The function assumes that the input stream is a valid iterable of numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = 0.0\n    count = 0\n    for value in stream:\n        total += value\n        count += 1\n    return total / count if count > 0 else 0.0\n```",
